                                  value = "Capability asks what an agent can bring about. Permission asks which actions are legitimate. Responsibility asks what the situation calls for among those possibilities. The kenotic synthesis separates these questions before developing its account of divine action."
                                }),
                              list("LiteralValue", {
                                  value = "The distinction also supplies an editorial question for machine delegation. A system may be able to generate a proposal, alter a record or carry out a plan. That ability alone cannot settle who should authorize the act or remain answerable for its consequences."
                                }),
