                        value = list("List", {
                            elements = list(
                              list("LiteralValue", {
                                  value = "Programme algebra is a parallel representation of the corpus. Its declared purpose is to preserve structure, provenance and refused transformations in a compositional grammar. The prose sources retain their authority; a generated projection does not become an independently editable truth."
                                }),
                              list("LiteralValue", {
                                  value = "The source distinguishes several depths. Recording a document and its links is different from admitting a scientific transformation. A protocol can contain all required fields without the experiment ever having run. These differences need to survive the trip into a more convenient view."
                                }),
                              list("LiteralValue", {
                                  value = "Apply the same question to this expedition. A station is an authored reading, a passage is a proposed connection, and a field note describes its source and limit. Following a path does not prove the connection. This map owes you a way to see that distinction."
